# Building an LRU Cache in Rust: A Comprehensive Tutorial

This tutorial walks through implementing a production-quality LRU (Least Recently Used) cache in Rust from scratch. We'll cover the generic data structure, all methods, error handling, memory-safety reasoning, concurrency options, complexity analysis, and worked examples. By the end, you'll have a fully functional cache with unit tests.

